I have an application that I've ported from a VMS-VAX to a VMS-Alpha.
The application involves both C modules and FORTRAN modules.  There is
a FORTRAN common in the program with various structures and variables.
There are various EXTERNS in the C modules which relate to the
structures in the FORTRAN common.
The program compiles, links, and runs on a VAX just fine.  On the
Alpha, the program will compile OK, but the linker complains about
some undefined symbols, which happen to be structures in the
FORTRAN common.  This program was written by myself (a FORTRAN
programmer) and a co-worker (a C programmer) who is no longer here.  I
dragged another C programmer into my office and he took a look at the
source code with me.  He says the problem is that the EXTERNS in the C
modules that I'm linking with the FORTRAN modules are not seeing the
symbols declared in the FORTRAN common.

I dragged out my Linker manual (may 1993) on page 2-2 it mentions some
stuff that sounds like what I'm doing.

From the book:
"In some Digital programming languages, certain types of global
symbols, such as external variables in C and COMMON data in FORTRAN,
are not listed in the GSD as global symbol references or definitions.
Because these data types implement virtual memory that is shared, the
languages implement them as program sections that are overlaid.  These
symbols appear as program section definitions in the GSD, not as
symbol definitions or reference. (Compilers use program sections to
define the memory requirements of an object module.)  The linker does
not include program section definitions in its symbol resoultion
processing.  For information about how the linker processes program
sections, see Chapter 3."

Well, I read chapter 3 and can not find a soultion for my problem.  I
assume all I need to do is add some lines to the linker options file
for the program, but I don't know that they may be.  Does anybody
out there know what I have to add to the linker options file so I can
link this thing?  

This is real important to me and I will appreciate any insight anyone
can give me.
Thanks,

Steve Kulpa
Project Leader
Environmental Systems Corp.
Knoxville, TN

Please remove the N*O*_S*P*A*M_ from my e-mail address
before replying to me directly.  Thanks!




